WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.799
Let's import an XLSX

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:07.520
file and turn it into a data table in

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.440
hacks.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.920
To perform this action, let's put the

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.519
page in edit mode by clicking the

00:00:13.519 --> 00:00:15.519
pencil.

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:20.160
Then let's get our XLSX file

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.960
and drop it onto Merlin or the search

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.279
bar up top. From there, we'll get a

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:27.199
series of options because it's detected

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:30.720
that it's an XLSX file. In this case,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.640
insert as table, insert as CSV text,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.879
link to the file, or just upload it and

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:40.719
not do anything.

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:44.719
Let's do insert as table.

00:00:44.719 --> 00:00:47.039
Instantly, it's taking the contents of

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:49.520
that file and importing them into the

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.199
page for us as a highly accessible

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:55.760
table. If I was to rightclick and

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.239
inspect, we can see under view source,

00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:00.559
it's created a table, imported the

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:03.840
headings, and put the content in place.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.080
In this case, this content is in a

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.000
format where we could actually import

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.799
and create a brand new site using this

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:13.439
file.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:16.240
So this is me saving that into one page.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.479
Or if I wanted to build a new site, if I

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:24.320
go down to import, we have Excel as one

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.920
of our imports. So if I have this file

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.640
format with the import from Excel,

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.680
now we've actually taken that XLSX file

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.799
from before, built out a site hierarchy

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:40.799
from it.
